{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HEB",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this Melchisedec, king of Salem, priest of the most high God, who met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings, and blessed him;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom also Abraham gave a tenth part of all; first being by interpretation King of righteousness, and after that also King of Salem, which is, King of peace;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Without father, without mother, without descent, having neither beginning of days, nor end of life; but made like to the Son of God; abideth a priest continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now consider how great this man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", to whom even the patriarch Abraham gave the tenth of the spoils.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And verily they that are of the sons of Levi, who receive the office of the priesthood, have a commandment to take tithes from the people according to the law, that is, from their brethren, though they come from the loins of Abraham:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he whose descent is not counted from them received tithes from Abraham, and blessed him that had the promises.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And without all contradiction the less is blessed by the better.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And here men that die receive tithes; but there he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "receiveth them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", of whom it is testified that he liveth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as I may say, Levi also, who receiveth tithes, payed tithes in Abraham.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he was yet in the loins of his father, when Melchisedec met him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If therefore perfection were by the Levitical priesthood (for under it the people received the law) what further need ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that another priest should rise after the order of Melchisedec, and not be called after the order of Aaron?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the priesthood being changed, there is made of necessity a change also of the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he of whom these things are spoken pertaineth to another tribe, of which no man gave attendance at the altar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " evident that our Lord sprang from Judah; of which tribe Moses spoke nothing concerning priesthood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it is yet far more evident: for that after the similitude of Melchisedec there ariseth another priest,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who is made, not after the law of a carnal commandment, but after the power of an endless life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he testifieth, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For there is verily a disannulling of the preceding commandment on account of its weakness and unprofitableness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the law made nothing perfect, but the introduction of a better hope ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "did",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; by which we draw nigh to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And inasmuch as not without an oath ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he was made priest",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For those priests were made without an oath; but this with an oath, by him that said to him, The Lord swore, and will not repent, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By so much was Jesus made a surety of a better testament.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they truly were many priests, because they were not suffered to continue by reason of death:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", because he continueth ever, hath an unchangeable priesthood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come to God by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For such a high priest became us, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy, harmless, undefiled, separate from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who needeth not daily, as those high priests, to offer up sacrifice, first for his own sins, and then for the people's: for this he did once, when he offered up himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.7.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.7.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the law maketh men high priests who have infirmity; but the word of the oath, which was after the law, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "maketh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Son, who is consecrated for evermore.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
